Physical follow-up found that POSIX AIO accepted only the first few 8 KB
format writes on iOS, leaving 24/64 KB partial images. On iOS only,
kabufuda's POSIX backend now completes each `pread`/`pwrite` synchronously;
other platforms retain AIO. Launch replaces only zero-megabit partial images.
The attached-iPad readback after the fix was 16,777,216 bytes for both A and B.
